# MITRE ATT&CK T1098.007 — Additional Local or Domain Groups

## ATT&CK Reference

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Tactics | Persistence / Privilege Escalation |
| Technique | Account Manipulation |
| Sub-technique | Additional Local or Domain Groups |
| Technique ID | T1098.007 |
| Lab Detection | DET-005 — Privileged Domain Group Membership Change |
| Primary Telemetry | Windows Security Event ID 4728 |
| SIEM | Splunk Enterprise |
| Status | Validated |

Official MITRE ATT&CK reference:

[T1098.007 — Additional Local or Domain Groups](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1098/007/)

---

# Technique Overview

Account privileges can be modified by changing membership in local or domain security groups.

Within an Active Directory environment, membership in highly privileged groups can significantly increase an account's capabilities.

Examples include:

```text
Domain Admins
Enterprise Admins
Schema Admins
```

Sprint 23 focuses on:

```text
Domain Account
      |
      v
Added to Privileged Domain Group
      |
      v
Privilege Change
```

This behavior maps to:

```text
T1098.007
Account Manipulation:
Additional Local or Domain Groups
```

