# Primary Telemetry

Sprint 23 uses:

```text
Windows Security Event ID 4728
```

Event meaning:

```text
A member was added to a security-enabled global group.
```

Important event context includes:

```text
Actor
Added Member
Target Group
Domain
Timestamp
Security Identifiers
```

---

# Event Relationships

A group membership event can be understood as:

```text
SUBJECT
Who made the change?
      |
      v
ACTION
Added member
      |
      v
MEMBER
Who received access?
      |
      v
TARGET GROUP
Which group granted access?
```

For the lab:

```text
Authorized Administrator
        |
        v
Adds det005test
        |
        v
Domain Admins
```

---

# DET-005

Detection:

```text
DET-005 — Privileged Domain Group Membership Change
```

Initial SPL:

```spl
index=* EventCode=4728 "Domain Admins"
```

Expanded SPL:

```spl
index=* EventCode=4728
("Domain Admins" OR "Enterprise Admins" OR "Schema Admins")
```

Portfolio output:

```spl
index=* EventCode=4728
("Domain Admins" OR "Enterprise Admins" OR "Schema Admins")
| eval detection="DET-005 - Privileged Domain Group Membership Change"
| table _time detection host _raw
```

---

# Controlled Validation

A dedicated domain account was used:

```text
CORP\det005test
```

Baseline:

```text
det005test
     |
     X
Domain Admins
```

Controlled modification:

```powershell
Add-ADGroupMember -Identity "Domain Admins" -Members det005test
```

Result:

```text
det005test
     |
     v
Domain Admins
```

The modification generated the security telemetry used to validate DET-005.

---

# Positive Validation

The account was removed and re-added to generate a fresh event.

```powershell
Remove-ADGroupMember -Identity "Domain Admins" -Members det005test -Confirm:$false
```

```powershell
Add-ADGroupMember -Identity "Domain Admins" -Members det005test
```

Detection result:

```text
DET-005 TRIGGERED
```

**Result:** PASS

---

# Negative Validation

A non-privileged security group was created:

```text
DET005-NormalGroup
```

The account was added to that group.

```powershell
Add-ADGroupMember -Identity "DET005-NormalGroup" -Members det005test
```

The membership change generated telemetry, but DET-005 did not identify it as a privileged-group addition.

```text
Normal Group Addition
        |
        v
Event 4728
        |
        v
Not Privileged
        |
        v
NO DET-005
```

**Result:** PASS

