Broader group-addition hunting:

```spl
index=* (EventCode=4728 OR EventCode=4732 OR EventCode=4756)
```

Saved as:

```text
HUNT - Security Group Membership Additions
```

Conceptually:

```text
All Security Group Additions
          |
          v
Identify Target Group
          |
          v
Identify Added Account
          |
          v
Identify Actor
          |
          v
Determine Risk
```

---

# Detection vs. Hunting

```text
DET-005
Privileged Groups Only
        |
        v
High-Severity Alert
```

versus:

```text
HUNT
All Security Group Additions
        |
        v
Analyst Review
```

---

# False Positive Analysis

Legitimate privileged-group additions may include:

```text
Administrator Onboarding
Temporary Elevation
Break-Glass Access
Emergency Maintenance
Infrastructure Changes
Service Configuration
Approved Access Changes
Security Testing
```

Therefore:

```text
Domain Admin Addition
        !=
Confirmed Account Compromise
```

But the potential impact justifies rapid review.

---

# Detection Confidence

### Base Signal

```text
Privileged Group Addition
```

### Increased Risk

```text
Privileged Group Addition
        +
New Account
```

### Higher Risk

```text
Privileged Group Addition
        +
New Account
        +
Recent Failed Authentication
```

### Strong Correlation

```text
Authentication Anomaly
        +
Suspicious PowerShell
        +
Persistence Activity
        +
Privileged Group Addition
        |
        v
High Investigative Priority
```

---

# Severity

DET-005 severity:

```text
HIGH
```

Rationale:

A privileged group membership change can immediately grant substantial access.

The detection therefore deserves rapid analyst review even though legitimate changes are possible.

